iterations.reply:
I left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem authority, which the node doesn't have, and calling the metadata service needs `aap:caps/http-client`, which isn't granted either. Adding either import would give the node authority its contract doesn't include. If operations needs logging or enrichment, it needs a node whose `with` clause grants that capability.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation = crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // Postcondition: delivered == true and session is present (non-empty).
        // A violating confirmation is never returned; the node traps instead.
        if !confirmation.delivered || confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("SendReply: postcondition violated");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

